    {
      "id": "p0079-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Incidentally, it wasn't actually necessary to change the naming screen for the Japanese release. For technical, historical, and linguistic reasons, English-only naming screens are quite common in Japanese games. But because this naming screen is one of the first player interactions in Undertale, 8-4's team put the extra work into improving the user interface.",
        "raw": "Incidentally, it wasn't actually necessary to change the naming screen for the\nJapanese release. For technical, historical, and linguistic reasons, English-only\nnaming screens are quite common in Japanese games. But because this naming\nscreen is one of the first player interactions in Undertale, 8-4's team put the\nextra work into improving the user interface.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09033191,
          0.48113571,
          0.69946288,
          0.56625
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
