    {
      "id": "p0079-b012",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In English, these seasonal quotes feel like short, silly sentences and mini poems. With that in mind, the translator localized the quotes as funny haiku poems while retaining the meaning of the original English quotes. Because haiku poems traditionally include references to seasons and nature, this localization choice turned out to be a natural fit for the Japanese release.",
        "raw": "In English, these seasonal quotes feel like short, silly sentences and mini\npoems. With that in mind, the translator localized the quotes as funny haiku\npoems while retaining the meaning of the original English quotes. Because\nhaiku poems traditionally include references to seasons and nature, this\nlocalization choice turned out to be a natural fit for the Japanese release.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
